ate network, answered by only one of them at a time\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"keepalived/VRRP configured via UCI on both nodes with virtual_ipaddress 10.100.179.50/24; direct evidence shows node1 (MASTER) holding the VIP on br-lan while node2 (BACKUP) does not have it assigned at the same timestamp.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-69c831313b054b78\",\"cmd-e8baa32c99324ed8\",\"cmd-0f63f13c7757492f\",\"cmd-98f969f5156d442b\"]},{\"id\":\"automatic-takeover\",\"requirement\":\"The other node takes over the address automatically when the first stops serving\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Stopping keepalived on node1 (MASTER) immediately resulted in node2 (BACKUP) acquiring the VIP without manual intervention, observed within seconds via ip addr checks.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-b76ef2f747d94f9d\",\"cmd-73fe932cfaea4ccd\"]},{\"id\":\"node3-continuous-reachability\",\"requirement\":\"node3 keeps reaching the shared address across one such transition\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A continuous background ping from node3 spanning the node1-to-node2 failover shows all icmp_seq 1-57 eventually answered (only a transient latency spike/reordering around the cutover, no dropped packets), directly demonstrating uninterrupted reachability across the transition.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-8feefec2b1c440eb\",\"cmd-6f61c576f0564472\",\"cmd-43b35df81f73487d\",\"cmd-9eb22895d53a4b6c\"]},{\"id\":\"restore-stable-state\",\"requirement\":\"Restore original component and confirm a stable redundant pair afterward\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node1's keepalived was restarted and preempted the VIP back (higher priority MASTER), node2 returned to clean BACKUP without the VIP, and node3 continued reaching the VIP successfully.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-21fc1fe7f1b44e04\",\"cmd-f4212c0ba9b44f91\",\"cmd-141d3b5a5f664a80\",\"cmd-71220eeb12f8492a\"]},{\"id\":\"mandatory-node-restart-protocol\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on every managed node (node1, node2, node3) with pre-restart identity/health, reboot ack, changed post-restart boot identity, and recovered service/cluster state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"All three nodes show pre-restart boot_id + health, an explicit reboot/systemctl reboot acknowledgement, polling through a connection outage, a new distinct post-restart boot_id, and recovered keepalived/VIP/ping state. Rebooting node1 (the then-MASTER) triggered a second live failover to node2 which was also captured with zero-loss pings from node3, then preemption back to node1 after recovery. Minor caveat: the fixed after-executor snapshot captured node1's boot-identity and node2's platform check mid-transition (return code 255), but this is superseded by the executor's own successful boot-id reads immediately afterward in the command timeline.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-3d5dc6a8e0194bcf\",\"cmd-3de62daa7385462f\",\"cmd-e93aa7179d0f43ae\",\"cmd-3d5196156ef44463\",\"cmd-e2fd544d19344cad\",\"cmd-9ae228a9ab414f2b\",\"cmd-624c17faf46c48fd\",\"cmd-8123ca5e931741f7\",\"cmd-7e234276ee5d4db7\",\"cmd-e1f8c60b0b5c4108\",\"cmd-308a25a0c4204494\",\"cmd-f78fef9104074bc0\",\"cmd-6cf113bf181b4c3e\",\"cmd-cc2b25ddf55f4d70\",\"cmd-291553469310460e\",\"cmd-faa7e40005404f40\",\"cmd-9350a9445d3d4c62\",\"cmd-0d4b532c19064547\",\"cmd-07c57fbbf08f40de\",\"cmd-a082c466122c411c\",\"cmd-097c51253441460f\",\"cmd-6227d2373955492b\",\"cmd-c694abec2a5a4d66\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.82,\"summary\":\"State-changing commands were largely well-justified: package installs (keepalived on both nodes), config writes (both the initial direct /etc/keepalived/keepalived.conf edits and the subsequent, authoritative UCI /etc/config/keepalived writes), service enable/restart/stop/start cycles for the failover demonstration, and three mandated reboots. One minor inefficiency: the executor first hand-edited /etc/keepalived/keepalived.conf directly (cmd-7de5bd9212ba4c1c on node1, cmd-8a42db6dc2ab4cd8 on node2) before discovering the UCI-managed init script overwrites /tmp/keepalived.conf from /etc/config/keepalived, and then redid the configuration properly via UCI (cmd-4e62b97d32bb4997, cmd-111278b7186d4800). This left an unused, superseded /etc/keepalived/keepalived.conf file on both nodes — bounded, low-risk residue rather than a functional problem. A background ping process was left running on node3 with /tmp/vip_ping.log and /tmp/vip_ping.pid not cleaned up after the demonstration (visible in the after-executor temp-files snapshot for node3), a small piece of abandoned diagnostic residue. No destructive actions, no weakened security controls, no failed services, and package-health diffs on node1/node2 show only the expected 'keepalived' uci-defaults addition.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-7de5bd9212ba4c1c\",\"cmd-8a42db6dc2ab4cd8\",\"cmd-4e62b97d32bb4997\",\"cmd-111278b7186d4800\",\"global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor configured a VRRP/keepalived-based shared VIP (10.100.179.50) between node1 and node2 via OpenWrt UCI, demonstrated automatic, zero-packet-loss failover to node3's continuous ping across a node1-stop/node2-takeover transition, restored node1 as MASTER, and confirmed a stable redundant end state. It also completed the mandatory provider-wide restart protocol on all three nodes with clear pre/post boot-identity changes, reboot acknowledgements, and recovered service/VIP/reachability state, including capturing a second live failover during node1's own reboot. All material task outcomes are directly satisfied by evidence.\",\"limitations\":[\"The fixed after-executor lifecycle snapshot captured node1's boot-identity check and node2's platform check mid-reboot/mid-transition (return code 255); this is superseded by successful boot-id reads in the executor's own command timeline shortly after, but it means the fixed snapshot alone cannot independently confirm final steady-state for those two specific checks.\",\"The /etc/keepalived/keepalived.conf file (manually edited before the UCI-based approach was adopted) was left in place on node1 and node2 but is unused since the init script regenerates /tmp/keepalived.conf from UCI; this is dead but harmless residue.\",\"A background ping process log/pid file (/tmp/vip_ping.log, /tmp/vip_ping.pid) was left on node3 after the demonstration rather than cleaned up.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"shared-vip-single-owner","requirement":"node1 and node2 share a single address on the private network, answered by only one of them at a time","status":"satisfied","summary":"keepalived/VRRP configured via UCI on both nodes with virtual_ipaddress 10.100.179.50/24; direct evidence shows node1 (MASTER) holding the VIP on br-lan while node2 (BACKUP) does not have it assigned at the same timestamp.","evidence_ids":["cmd-69c831313b054b78","cmd-e8baa32c99324ed8","cmd-0f63f13c7757492f","cmd-98f969f5156d442b"]},{"id":"automatic-takeover","requirement":"The other node takes over the address automatically when the first stops serving","status":"satisfied","summary":"Stopping keepalived on node1 (MASTER) immediately resulted in node2 (BACKUP) acquiring the VIP without manual intervention, observed within seconds via ip addr checks.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b76ef2f747d94f9d","cmd-73fe932cfaea4ccd"]},{"id":"node3-continuous-reachability","requirement":"node3 keeps reaching the shared address across one such transition","status":"satisfied","summary":"A continuous background ping from node3 spanning the node1-to-node2 failover shows all icmp_seq 1-57 eventually answered (only a transient latency spike/reordering around the cutover, no dropped packets), directly demonstrating uninterrupted reachability across the transition.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8feefec2b1c440eb","cmd-6f61c576f0564472","cmd-43b35df81f73487d","cmd-9eb22895d53a4b6c"]},{"id":"restore-stable-state","requirement":"Restore original component and c