irectly satisfied by evidence.","limitations":["The fixed after-executor lifecycle snapshot captured node1's boot-identity check and node2's platform check mid-reboot/mid-transition (return code 255); this is superseded by successful boot-id reads in the executor's own command timeline shortly after, but it means the fixed snapshot alone cannot independently confirm final steady-state for those two specific checks.","The /etc/keepalived/keepalived.conf file (manually edited before the UCI-based approach was adopted) was left in place on node1 and node2 but is unused since the init script regenerates /tmp/keepalived.conf from UCI; this is dead but harmless residue.","A background ping process log/pid file (/tmp/vip_ping.log, /tmp/vip_ping.pid) was left on node3 after the demonstration rather than cleaned up."]},"ttft_ms":26335,"type":"result","duration_ms":82837,"uuid":"9b84e957-b15a-481a-82e5-cdee01d9753c","ttft_stream_ms":3623,"time_to_request_ms":40,"first_content_frame_ms":4364,"queued_turn_count":0}
